Not really. The main point of save scumming is to take back a sequence of
moves if the player has made a mistake. In the case of bicycle riding,
you are constantly making progress toward your goal. The difference
between a "Century" and riding 100 miles in a week is purely
quantitative. The whole issue of "reverting back to a state before the
error" is lost in the analogy.

I still think that "chess against a computer program" is the best analogy
(see also <b37690$1j03hn$1@ID-3042.news.dfncis.de>).

